# First-class continuations in eric-lang
# Because a stack-based language clearly needs call/cc

# Simple example: callcc captures "what happens next"
# and stores it for later use

add(1, 2)
print

# In the principled rewrite, every intermediate value
# is a thunk, every function call goes through unification,
# and the continuation is always available.
# This is what "addressing review feedback" looks like.
